# Paths cakebear owns.
#
# Everything else in this repository belongs to upstream (microsoft/TypeScript's
# Go compiler, the tsc/ directory of that repo) and is replaced wholesale by
# every sync. Never edit it: see CLAUDE.md, "The golden rule", for why. A file
# cakebear writes outside these paths is deleted by the next sync.
#
# One path per line. A trailing slash means "this directory and everything
# under it"; anything else is an exact file path. Blank lines and lines
# starting with # are ignored.
#
# Deliberately extensionless: it was silently untracked for five phases as
# owned-paths.txt, under the blanket `*.txt` ignore rule upstream used to ship.
# cakebear owns .gitignore now, but the name stays as it is.
#
# Read by:
#   scripts/check-upstream-untouched.sh  (fails a PR that touches upstream)
#   scripts/check-upstream-snapshot.sh   (upstream files equal the snapshot)
#   scripts/check-boundary.sh            (keeps ir/ and backend/ extractable)
#   scripts/check-line-limit.py          (only lints .go files we own)
#   scripts/owned-go-packages.sh         (test, coverage and lint scoping)
#   scripts/sync-upstream.sh             (never touches these paths)

cmd/cakec/
ir/
lower/
backend/
types/
examples/
scripts/
CLAUDE.md
README.md
